<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#reich-protector">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reich Protector</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1939–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Reichsprotektor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reich Protector, in German Reichsprotektor, was the title of the highest German official in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> from 1939 to 1945, who held real power over the nominal Czech government. The post was held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-von-neurath">Konstantin von Neurath</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reinhard-heydrich">Reinhard Heydrich</a> acting in his place from 1941 until his assassination in 1942, and then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-frick">Wilhelm Frick</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reich-protector.jpg" alt="Reich Protector" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Protectorate_of_Bohemia_and_Moravia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
